1
00:00:06,125 --> 00:00:07,166
A child?

2
00:00:08,083 --> 00:00:10,000
There's one more thing you should know.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,041
The majority of previous bloodsport champions

4
00:00:13,083 --> 00:00:15,125
have died during their final matches.

5
00:00:16,125 --> 00:00:18,208
I heard the duke running
the bloodsport colosseum

6
00:00:18,208 --> 00:00:21,041
arranges for the champions
to be at a disadvantage.

7
00:00:21,208 --> 00:00:24,041
Eve Speed is the undefeated champion

8
00:00:24,125 --> 00:00:26,000
and tremendously popular.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,166
Management would almost certainly

10
00:00:27,166 --> 00:00:30,125
want to kill her to pass the
baton to the next generation.

11
00:00:30,166 --> 00:00:34,125
Which means we'll be stopping
that tomorrow, right?

12
00:00:34,208 --> 00:00:37,000
No, that's not my intention.

13
00:00:37,208 --> 00:00:41,083
There's no need for us
to politely wait until the day of.

14
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,208
TOGETHER WITH THE LORD OF FLIES

15
00:02:16,166 --> 00:02:18,166
Did you need me for something?

16
00:02:19,125 --> 00:02:22,041
I came here to talk with you, Eve Speed.

17
00:02:22,166 --> 00:02:25,166
I thought I already told you I don't
know where the Witch of Taboos is.

18
00:02:25,208 --> 00:02:28,083
That was a lie, right?

19
00:02:28,083 --> 00:02:30,041
You're a rude man.

20
00:02:30,041 --> 00:02:31,083
You indebted to the witch?

21
00:02:31,125 --> 00:02:32,083
No.

22
00:02:32,208 --> 00:02:34,125
That was a lie just now.

23
00:02:34,125 --> 00:02:35,208
And who are you?

24
00:02:36,041 --> 00:02:40,041
Why don't we stop trying
to deceive each other, Eve Speed?

25
00:02:40,125 --> 00:02:42,041
Tell me what you're after.

26
00:02:42,083 --> 00:02:43,125
I want to save you.

27
00:02:44,083 --> 00:02:45,208
"Save" me?

28
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,125
The duke running the show will make sure
you go down in tomorrow's match.

29
00:02:52,041 --> 00:02:54,083
Why would you help me?

30
00:02:54,083 --> 00:02:58,000
Because I can't have someone with intel
on the Witch of Taboos dying on me.

31
00:02:58,166 --> 00:03:01,000
Is kidnapping the girl you brought to Monroy

32
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:03,125
and fleeing tonight not an option?

33
00:03:03,125 --> 00:03:04,166
Why you!

34
00:03:04,208 --> 00:03:06,125
If you dare lay a finger on that girl...

35
00:03:06,208 --> 00:03:09,208
I just wanted you to know I'm
aware of your situation.

36
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,125
We know you've been fighting
for Lis's sake these past two years.

37
00:03:17,083 --> 00:03:20,125
I appreciate the warning about the plot.

38
00:03:20,166 --> 00:03:24,083
However, I can't afford to run
from tomorrow's bloodsport.

39
00:03:24,125 --> 00:03:26,125
Why not agree to kidnap her and flee?

40
00:03:27,041 --> 00:03:28,125
Where would we flee to?

41
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:31,083
Unless I play by the rules
to gain her freedom,

42
00:03:31,083 --> 00:03:33,208
Duke Zuan will hunt us down,

43
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,041
the guild running the colosseum
will put up a bounty,

44
00:03:37,041 --> 00:03:41,000
and mercenaries across the
continent will come after us.

45
00:03:41,166 --> 00:03:43,125
It'd be one thing if it were just me,

46
00:03:43,125 --> 00:03:45,083
but I can't do that to that girl.

47
00:03:45,125 --> 00:03:47,125
What if I know a good place to hide?

48
00:03:48,083 --> 00:03:50,041
Where the Witch of Taboos lives.

49
00:03:50,125 --> 00:03:52,083
You could have her shelter you two.

50
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:54,000
Impossible.

51
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,125
No one can reach the heart
of the Land of Monsters.

52
00:03:56,166 --> 00:03:58,000
- The heart?
- I told you, it's not the kind of place
you just waltz into.

53
00:03:58,041 --> 00:04:01,000
- I told you, it's not the kind of place
you just waltz into.
- She's talking like she's been there before.

54
00:04:01,208 --> 00:04:04,166
If we work together,
we might able to reach it.

55
00:04:04,166 --> 00:04:07,125
I promise to protect that girl
to my fullest ability as well.

56
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:08,208
So, how about it?

57
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,125
Are you willing to wager on us?

58
00:04:12,041 --> 00:04:16,083
Your swordsman seems to have
martial training, but you...

59
00:04:17,041 --> 00:04:19,166
Despite appearances, I'm skilled with magic.

60
00:04:20,083 --> 00:04:23,125
I'm good enough I managed to defeat
a Skeleton King with ease.

61
00:04:23,125 --> 00:04:25,166
Those are certainly fierce,

62
00:04:25,208 --> 00:04:28,208
but they're nothing compared to what
lies within the Land of Monsters.

63
00:04:28,208 --> 00:04:32,208
Then what if I told you I was the
one who killed the Five Dragoons?

64
00:04:32,208 --> 00:04:34,000
Impossible.

65
00:04:34,041 --> 00:04:36,125
I don't know if this will
convince you, but...

66
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,041
Paralyze!

67
00:04:39,083 --> 00:04:40,083
My body...!

68
00:04:40,125 --> 00:04:42,041
You shouldn't try to move.

69
00:04:42,083 --> 00:04:46,208
If you force it, you'll begin
bleeding from various places.

70
00:04:46,208 --> 00:04:48,125
Absurd!

71
00:04:48,125 --> 00:04:49,125
Precisely.

72
00:04:49,208 --> 00:04:54,125
This absurd power is what allowed a
weakling like me to kill Civit Gartland.

73
00:04:54,125 --> 00:04:57,041
Allow me to provide additional proof.

74
00:04:57,041 --> 00:05:01,166
I'm Seras Ashrain, the one the
Five Dragoons were pursuing.

75
00:05:02,166 --> 00:05:06,125
I witnessed their deaths with my own eyes.

76
00:05:06,166 --> 00:05:08,208
It's up to you whether you believe us.

77
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,000
I just wanted to demonstrate my power

78
00:05:10,041 --> 00:05:11,083
DISMISS (HEAD)
- I just wanted to demonstrate my power

79
00:05:11,083 --> 00:05:13,041
DISMISS (HEAD)
- to prove myself to you.

80
00:05:13,208 --> 00:05:15,041
You certainly have.

81
00:05:15,166 --> 00:05:18,083
However, it's to no avail.

82
00:05:18,083 --> 00:05:21,125
Either way, I must face my
bloodsport match tomorrow.

83
00:05:21,125 --> 00:05:23,000
I won't go to the Land of Monsters.

84
00:05:23,041 --> 00:05:24,041
That remains unchanged.

85
00:05:24,083 --> 00:05:26,166
I will seize our freedom with my own hands.

86
00:05:27,041 --> 00:05:31,000
Victory in bloodsport has always
been my path forward.

87
00:05:31,041 --> 00:05:33,125
Besides, I can't fully trust you two.

88
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:36,083
Even though my liege wishes to save you?

89
00:05:36,083 --> 00:05:39,125
Would you believe someone
you'd only just met that day?

90
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:44,208
In contrast, bloodsport and I
have a long history together.

91
00:05:45,041 --> 00:05:47,000
Well, that's to be expected.

92
00:05:47,125 --> 00:05:49,083
Still, even if you win the match,

93
00:05:49,125 --> 00:05:52,125
do you truly believe Duke Zuan
will keep his word?

94
00:05:52,125 --> 00:05:53,125
What?

95
00:05:53,125 --> 00:05:56,125
He sounds like a scumbag from
what I've heard about him.

96
00:05:56,208 --> 00:06:01,208
I find it hard to believe he'll
honestly just grant you your freedom.

97
00:06:02,041 --> 00:06:05,125
I know he's not a very upstanding man.

98
00:06:05,125 --> 00:06:09,125
But the fact is that he's always honored
his end when I produced results.

99
00:06:09,166 --> 00:06:10,208
The duke is still human.

100
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
I doubt he's as heartless as you claim.

101
00:06:13,041 --> 00:06:13,208
You're naive.

102
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:19,208
Between you two and the world of bloodsport,
it's obvious which I should trust more.

103
00:06:20,083 --> 00:06:22,166
I'll keep my faith in bloodsport.

104
00:06:23,041 --> 00:06:24,166
Why, Eve Speed?

105
00:06:25,166 --> 00:06:29,125
Why do you keep insisting
you believe in bloodsport?

106
00:06:29,166 --> 00:06:30,166
What?

107
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:35,125
Are you sure you aren't saying it
in order to convince yourself?

108
00:06:37,083 --> 00:06:39,083
I know I've said a few rude things,

109
00:06:39,083 --> 00:06:42,083
but I'll genuinely be praying
for your victory tomorrow.

110
00:06:42,208 --> 00:06:44,166
- Let's go.
- Y-Yes.

111
00:06:45,125 --> 00:06:47,083
Wait! Why are you—

112
00:06:48,166 --> 00:06:52,041
We plan to leave the city
early tomorrow morning.

113
00:06:52,041 --> 00:06:54,041
We'll be at the bridge by the big front gate.

114
00:06:54,125 --> 00:06:56,166
You should come if you change your mind.

115
00:07:01,083 --> 00:07:02,208
My apologies.

116
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,166
I revealed my identity without asking.

117
00:07:06,083 --> 00:07:09,166
In the end, it made our
argument more convincing.

118
00:07:10,041 --> 00:07:11,166
I'm not concerned about it.

119
00:07:13,125 --> 00:07:15,083
Did something happen here?

120
00:07:15,125 --> 00:07:19,208
Those in this home have been cursed
for the sin of defying Sir Muaji,

121
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,208
progeny of the curse god.

122
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:22,208
Muaji?

123
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,125
The Five Dragoons fell to our curses!

124
00:07:24,125 --> 00:07:26,041
- The Five Dragoons fell to our curses!
- They say the man of the house
was foaming at the mouth

125
00:07:26,041 --> 00:07:27,125
- They say the man of the house
was foaming at the mouth
- We are the saviors of Ulza!

126
00:07:27,125 --> 00:07:29,166
- We are the saviors of Ulza!
- and clawing at his throat as he died.

127
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,041
I'm sure he must have been cursed.

128
00:07:32,083 --> 00:07:33,208
How scary.

129
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,125
I find myself outraged at their insolence.

130
00:07:37,125 --> 00:07:38,208
It seems like those guys

131
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:41,041
genuinely believe their group
took out the Five Dragoons.

132
00:07:41,083 --> 00:07:43,125
- genuinely believe their group
took out the Five Dragoons.
- P-Please stop this!

133
00:07:43,125 --> 00:07:45,000
Consider it an honor.

134
00:07:45,041 --> 00:07:47,125
You've been chosen by us.

135
00:07:47,125 --> 00:07:48,125
It's a glorious thing.

136
00:07:48,166 --> 00:07:50,125
Now, come along quietly.

137
00:07:50,125 --> 00:07:52,125
Please! Please let go of me!

138
00:07:52,125 --> 00:07:54,166
This simply won't do.

139
00:07:54,166 --> 00:07:56,208
We must take you to Sir Muaji and beg for him

140
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:00,000
to show you his blessing
and reform your heart!

141
00:08:00,208 --> 00:08:02,000
Don't lay a hand on them.

142
00:08:02,125 --> 00:08:03,125
Berserk.

143
00:08:07,041 --> 00:08:08,041
Hey! Stop!

144
00:08:08,083 --> 00:08:09,083
- What's gotten into you?!
- Dark. Berserk. Berserk.

145
00:08:09,125 --> 00:08:10,125
Dark. Berserk. Berserk.

146
00:08:11,041 --> 00:08:13,000
Y-You too?!

147
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,208
What the hell is going on here?!

148
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:15,208
Right.

149
00:08:22,125 --> 00:08:24,125
Roughly four hours until time's up.

150
00:08:24,125 --> 00:08:26,083
Do you think there's a future

151
00:08:26,125 --> 00:08:29,125
where she wins their freedom and
lives peacefully with that girl?

152
00:08:29,125 --> 00:08:30,125
Nope.

153
00:08:30,166 --> 00:08:35,083
From what people have said, Eve's owner,
Duke Zuan, is a piece of shit.

154
00:08:35,083 --> 00:08:37,208
There's no bright future
for her with him around.

155
00:08:38,083 --> 00:08:41,083
I'd never trust someone
I deem to be a scumbag.

156
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,166
So long as Eve Speed remains
a good, honest person,

157
00:08:44,166 --> 00:08:47,083
there is no happy ending for her here.

158
00:08:48,041 --> 00:08:50,208
Not until someone comes along with a poison

159
00:08:51,166 --> 00:08:54,208
strong enough to counteract
the poison already eating away at her.

160
00:08:56,208 --> 00:09:00,083
I've more than fulfilled my
obligations to Duke Zuan.

161
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
He should be satisfied.

162
00:09:03,166 --> 00:09:06,166
Surely he'll show mercy
in honor of my contributions.

163
00:09:14,041 --> 00:09:15,208
I'm only going to confirm that.

164
00:09:15,208 --> 00:09:19,125
To confirm that I'll be free
if I win tomorrow.

165
00:09:19,125 --> 00:09:22,041
Then I'll be rid of this doubt.

166
00:09:24,083 --> 00:09:29,041
I imagine tomorrow will be a grand event
with Eve Speed's final bloodsport match.

167
00:09:29,083 --> 00:09:30,083
Yes.

168
00:09:30,083 --> 00:09:34,000
We don't have any other bloodsport
warriors so beloved by the crowd.

169
00:09:34,041 --> 00:09:36,083
See? They aren't plotting any—

170
00:09:36,125 --> 00:09:39,166
So, Eve Speed will die as planned, yes?

171
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,208
Of course.

172
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,208
Per tradition, we'll give her
a paralytic before the match.

173
00:09:46,208 --> 00:09:48,125
The goblet of purification?

174
00:09:48,166 --> 00:09:50,083
That was a great idea.

175
00:09:51,208 --> 00:09:54,083
DUKE ZUAN
- I've already given that mangy pseudo-human
plenty of chances to shine.

176
00:09:54,125 --> 00:09:57,000
I've already given that mangy pseudo-human
plenty of chances to shine.

177
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:59,041
Yet she's still a beast in the end.

178
00:09:59,041 --> 00:10:04,041
Let's have tomorrow's victor
skin her hide and wear it.

179
00:10:04,041 --> 00:10:05,125
Wonderful idea!

180
00:10:05,166 --> 00:10:08,041
We can sell them as the Leopard Slayer!

181
00:10:10,208 --> 00:10:14,000
Well, what about that dark elf
at the Whiteleg Tavern?

182
00:10:14,083 --> 00:10:18,166
Eve kept at bloodsport much longer
than we planned thanks to her.

183
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:19,166
So what are your plans?

184
00:10:19,208 --> 00:10:22,125
Will you be granting her
freedom as an act of mercy?

185
00:10:22,166 --> 00:10:26,208
Actually, I'll be taking her in.

186
00:10:26,208 --> 00:10:29,208
Oh? Showing some compassion?

187
00:10:29,208 --> 00:10:32,083
She's just a childish brat right now,

188
00:10:32,125 --> 00:10:35,000
but she'll be an incredible beauty one day.

189
00:10:35,041 --> 00:10:38,041
I plan to thoroughly train her myself.

190
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:42,166
If I tire of her, then I'll simply
sell her off to a whorehouse.

191
00:10:43,208 --> 00:10:48,000
Still, haven't you spent a
long time with Eve as well?

192
00:10:48,041 --> 00:10:49,125
Have you no sympathy for her?

193
00:10:49,125 --> 00:10:52,083
Now that's an odd thing to ask.

194
00:10:52,125 --> 00:10:57,041
How could I ever develop any sympathy
for a subhuman animal?

195
00:10:57,083 --> 00:10:59,083
Duke Zuan...

196
00:10:59,125 --> 00:11:01,208
You're truly a brute so vile?!

197
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,166
Unless I rescue her,
there is no escape for her.

198
00:11:15,208 --> 00:11:17,166
Lady Eve Speed.

199
00:11:17,166 --> 00:11:18,125
Hmm?

200
00:11:18,166 --> 00:11:20,000
I'm looking forward

201
00:11:20,125 --> 00:11:23,083
MUAJI
ASHINT'S LEADER
- to tomorrow's bloodsport match.

202
00:11:23,208 --> 00:11:24,208
Yeah.

203
00:11:25,208 --> 00:11:27,166
So this is where you were!

204
00:11:27,208 --> 00:11:28,166
Sir Muaji!

205
00:11:28,208 --> 00:11:30,083
There's been some trouble...

206
00:11:37,125 --> 00:11:39,041
Have they left already?

207
00:11:43,041 --> 00:11:45,000
You're earlier than I expected.

208
00:11:45,041 --> 00:11:46,125
If you're here, then...

209
00:11:46,125 --> 00:11:49,000
Yes, it was exactly as you said.

210
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:51,125
So, are we bringing that girl with us?

211
00:11:51,166 --> 00:11:52,125
Of course.

212
00:11:52,166 --> 00:11:55,125
I can't afford to leave her here.

213
00:11:55,125 --> 00:11:59,125
Then can I assume you're going
to the Land of Monsters with us?

214
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:05,000
I have my terms, but I intend
to tell you where the witch lives.

215
00:12:05,041 --> 00:12:07,041
Then it's settled.

216
00:12:07,083 --> 00:12:10,083
Now, let's get to kidnapping.

217
00:12:13,041 --> 00:12:14,000
Lis!

218
00:12:14,041 --> 00:12:16,208
You're still cleaning that spot?

219
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,041
You're so slow!

220
00:12:18,083 --> 00:12:23,041
You dark elves really
are useless, aren't you?

221
00:12:23,041 --> 00:12:25,000
I'm sorry...

222
00:12:25,208 --> 00:12:28,166
This girl's starting to get
a little sexy too, isn't she?

223
00:12:28,208 --> 00:12:29,166
Hey, you!

224
00:12:29,166 --> 00:12:31,083
You'll pay if you lay a hand on her!

225
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:35,125
Someone important has already agreed
to take in this brat one day, you hear?

226
00:12:35,125 --> 00:12:39,000
Tch. Damn brat, already seducing people...

227
00:12:39,125 --> 00:12:41,125
Still, she's a real quiet one, ain't she?

228
00:12:41,166 --> 00:12:43,125
Never smiles and never cries.

229
00:12:43,166 --> 00:12:45,083
You sure she even has emotions?

230
00:12:45,083 --> 00:12:49,000
You would think, but—up we go—the
brat is really just toughing it out.

231
00:12:49,041 --> 00:12:51,083
There! There! There! There!

232
00:12:52,041 --> 00:12:55,125
Now, I wonder how long you can endure.

233
00:12:56,125 --> 00:12:58,083
She may seem unfazed,

234
00:12:58,083 --> 00:13:00,083
but it's having a sure effect on her.

235
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,041
This is for me?

236
00:13:03,083 --> 00:13:04,041
Yeah.

237
00:13:04,083 --> 00:13:06,041
We'll fight together,

238
00:13:06,041 --> 00:13:08,083
and together we'll win our freedom.

239
00:13:09,083 --> 00:13:12,125
I need to be strong, like Big Sis.

240
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:15,166
Wasn't that a bit harsh?

241
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:18,083
I'm the one people should feel sorry for!

242
00:13:18,125 --> 00:13:21,125
I'm working myself to the bone,
and no good comes of it!

243
00:13:21,166 --> 00:13:25,041
What's wrong with venting a
little pent-up stress on the brat?

244
00:13:25,083 --> 00:13:27,125
Tch! Already stopped her damn crying.

245
00:13:27,125 --> 00:13:30,083
I know what you hate most.

246
00:13:31,125 --> 00:13:33,125
Don't overdo it now.

247
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,166
Get a big head and I'll kill you,
you damn brat!

248
00:13:37,208 --> 00:13:40,166
I'm sorry for being weak, Big Sis...

249
00:13:44,125 --> 00:13:46,166
I never heard it was this bad.

250
00:13:49,208 --> 00:13:51,041
Big Sis...

251
00:13:51,125 --> 00:13:52,208
It's over now.

252
00:13:52,208 --> 00:13:55,000
I'm taking the girl with me.

253
00:13:55,041 --> 00:13:56,041
And you...

254
00:13:56,208 --> 00:13:58,000
P-Please spare me!

255
00:13:58,041 --> 00:14:03,041
Duke Zuan ordered me
to discipline her harshly!

256
00:14:03,041 --> 00:14:05,208
If I'd refused, he would have killed me too!

257
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:06,208
I swear!

258
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,208
I won't say a word to anyone
about wherever you two go!

259
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,041
So please spare me!

260
00:14:13,208 --> 00:14:16,083
The situation's changed.
We can't stay in the capital now.

261
00:14:16,208 --> 00:14:20,041
It looks like I'll be taking you
with me on another harsh journey.

262
00:14:20,041 --> 00:14:22,000
Would you still come with me?

263
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:22,208
Yes.

264
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:26,125
I'll go anywhere as long
as I'm with you, Big Sis.

265
00:14:26,208 --> 00:14:29,041
You tell them that Eve Speed headed south

266
00:14:29,041 --> 00:14:32,083
to search for Lisbeth after
she suddenly disappeared.

267
00:14:32,125 --> 00:14:34,166
If you can do that, I'll spare you.

268
00:14:34,166 --> 00:14:37,083
G-Got it! I absolutely will!

269
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:40,125
I'll never forget your mercy in sparing me!

270
00:14:40,125 --> 00:14:43,041
Lis, I apologize for everything
I've done to you.

271
00:14:43,083 --> 00:14:45,000
Please forgive me.

272
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,208
I can't believe I was so
harsh to such a kind child.

273
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:51,083
Thank you for everything.

274
00:14:51,166 --> 00:14:53,125
Be well, Lis.

275
00:14:53,125 --> 00:14:54,166
We're going.

276
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:58,083
Big Sis! Is that...

277
00:15:03,125 --> 00:15:07,166
Sorry for suddenly making a loud noise.

278
00:15:07,166 --> 00:15:08,166
Go on ahead.

279
00:15:08,208 --> 00:15:11,000
I'll take care of some business and join you.

280
00:15:11,166 --> 00:15:12,166
All right.

281
00:15:13,041 --> 00:15:15,125
You may have fooled a good person like Eve,

282
00:15:15,166 --> 00:15:17,208
but your shitty acting won't work on me.

283
00:15:18,041 --> 00:15:20,208
Do you really think you're
going to get away with this?!

284
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,166
You're defying him!

285
00:15:22,166 --> 00:15:25,166
It's over! For you and that mangy beast!

286
00:15:26,125 --> 00:15:27,166
Serves you right!

287
00:15:27,208 --> 00:15:30,000
I could tell immediately
by that girl's reaction.

288
00:15:30,208 --> 00:15:33,208
It feels great to hit nearby
objects and raise hell

289
00:15:33,208 --> 00:15:36,125
when you're shouting and angry, doesn't it?

290
00:15:36,208 --> 00:15:39,125
But it's intolerable to
those on the receiving end.

291
00:15:39,125 --> 00:15:43,041
Any loud noise sends them right back
to every time you shouted at them.

292
00:15:43,208 --> 00:15:45,041
I can't stand it.

293
00:15:45,041 --> 00:15:46,041
What?

294
00:15:46,083 --> 00:15:50,083
I can't stand the idea of you getting
to live like nothing happened

295
00:15:50,083 --> 00:15:53,166
after all the horrible things
you did to that girl.

296
00:15:53,208 --> 00:15:56,208
I just told you it's all over for you lot!

297
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:00,166
I'm the only one who can save
you from that terrifying duke!

298
00:16:00,166 --> 00:16:03,083
So be clear! Are you begging
for my forgiveness or not?!

299
00:16:03,166 --> 00:16:05,166
I was already clear, wasn't I?

300
00:16:05,166 --> 00:16:08,083
It's over for you.

301
00:16:09,041 --> 00:16:10,041
Paralyze.

302
00:16:10,041 --> 00:16:11,125
Dark. Poison.

303
00:16:12,208 --> 00:16:14,208
Y-You monster...

304
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,166
Right back at you.

305
00:16:16,208 --> 00:16:18,125
It won't be a great cover,

306
00:16:18,125 --> 00:16:20,208
but I'll make it look like
you were a robbery victim.

307
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:26,000
If you do this, then you're
going straight to hell.

308
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,208
If you let me go, then you
can make it to heaven.

309
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,041
GATES OF HELL
- Hell? Heaven?

310
00:16:31,083 --> 00:16:33,083
GATES OF HELL
GATES OF HEAVEN
- Hell? Heaven?

311
00:16:33,083 --> 00:16:35,125
I'm willing to do whatever
it takes for my goals.

312
00:16:35,208 --> 00:16:37,208
I've roped other people into my revenge,

313
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,208
and I've already crushed plenty underfoot.

314
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,083
You must be stupid.

315
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:43,166
We're obviously going to hell.

316
00:16:44,083 --> 00:16:46,208
Both you and me.

317
00:16:56,125 --> 00:16:58,000
Sorry to keep you waiting.

318
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:58,208
It's fine.

319
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,041
Hati, I'm sorry about earlier.

320
00:17:01,208 --> 00:17:03,208
What happened with that woman?

321
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,166
I did what needed to be done.

322
00:17:05,208 --> 00:17:06,208
I see.

323
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,208
More importantly, is the girl okay?

324
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,041
Yeah. Lis, introduce yourself.

325
00:17:11,041 --> 00:17:12,208
M-My name is Lisbeth.

326
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,041
LISBETH
DARK ELF
- I'm sorry. I don't know my last name.

327
00:17:15,083 --> 00:17:16,208
I'm sorry. I don't know my last name.

328
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Oh, please call me Lis
since Lisbeth is so long.

329
00:17:20,041 --> 00:17:21,083
I'm Touka.

330
00:17:23,166 --> 00:17:25,041
Hati was an alias.

331
00:17:25,125 --> 00:17:27,166
My real name is Touka Mimori.

332
00:17:27,208 --> 00:17:30,083
And this swordswoman is Seras Ashrain.

333
00:17:30,166 --> 00:17:33,083
It's a pleasure to be with both of you.

334
00:17:33,166 --> 00:17:34,208
Sir Tooka...

335
00:17:34,208 --> 00:17:36,125
I'll do anything.

336
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:40,125
So please let me accompany Big Sis.

337
00:17:40,125 --> 00:17:42,041
Please.

338
00:17:42,125 --> 00:17:46,125
We're about to head into a dangerous
place where we might lose our lives.

339
00:17:46,125 --> 00:17:47,125
I don't care.

340
00:17:47,166 --> 00:17:49,083
As long as I'm with Big Sis.

341
00:17:52,208 --> 00:17:53,166
All right.

342
00:17:53,208 --> 00:17:55,166
Thank you so much!

343
00:17:55,208 --> 00:17:58,041
This has bugged me for a while,

344
00:17:58,041 --> 00:17:59,000
but Tooka,

345
00:17:59,041 --> 00:18:02,166
are you aware of an odd,
watery sound coming from your person?

346
00:18:02,166 --> 00:18:05,000
Yeah, that's my other companion.

347
00:18:05,041 --> 00:18:06,000
Companion?

348
00:18:06,041 --> 00:18:07,166
Introduce yourself, Piggymaru.

349
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,041
A slime?

350
00:18:12,083 --> 00:18:15,083
These are our new traveling
companions, Eve and Lisbeth.

351
00:18:15,083 --> 00:18:18,083
I'm Eve Speed. Good to meet you.

352
00:18:19,083 --> 00:18:22,041
It's nice to meet you, little Piggymaru.

353
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:31,166
I do intend to tell you where
the Witch of Taboos lives.

354
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,208
Though, before I do,

355
00:18:34,208 --> 00:18:37,000
I'd like to hear why you want to meet her.

356
00:18:38,125 --> 00:18:40,000
I have a scroll of forbidden magic

357
00:18:40,041 --> 00:18:42,125
written in ancient text that's
difficult to decipher.

358
00:18:42,125 --> 00:18:45,125
But I've heard the Witch of Taboos
should be able to do it.

359
00:18:46,041 --> 00:18:49,125
Then you don't intend her any harm?

360
00:18:50,041 --> 00:18:52,083
So long as she doesn't intend me any.

361
00:18:56,041 --> 00:18:58,041
I'm a simple woman.

362
00:18:58,083 --> 00:19:01,000
I can't read the far future like you can.

363
00:19:01,041 --> 00:19:04,083
I can't predict everything either.

364
00:19:04,083 --> 00:19:06,166
I'd like to swear myself to you.

365
00:19:06,208 --> 00:19:10,000
Wow, talk about a pretty big jump in trust.

366
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,125
I believe you are a trustworthy man.

367
00:19:12,166 --> 00:19:13,125
Your reasoning?

368
00:19:13,208 --> 00:19:16,166
You could have chosen any
number of inhumane means

369
00:19:16,208 --> 00:19:19,125
to get information on
the Witch of Taboos out of me.

370
00:19:19,208 --> 00:19:22,041
You could have used that girl
to threaten me as well.

371
00:19:22,083 --> 00:19:24,041
But you didn't.

372
00:19:24,083 --> 00:19:26,000
You are a good person.

373
00:19:27,125 --> 00:19:31,125
What happened to not trusting people
you only just met that day?

374
00:19:32,041 --> 00:19:35,166
Trustworthiness can't be determined
by the length of time you spend with someone.

375
00:19:35,208 --> 00:19:38,166
I feel like this has taught me that much.

376
00:19:41,041 --> 00:19:42,041
Take my hand.

377
00:19:42,083 --> 00:19:43,041
Sure.

378
00:19:43,041 --> 00:19:46,125
Will it be all right to take the girl
with us into the Land of Monsters?

379
00:19:46,208 --> 00:19:48,125
I'll protect her no matter what.

380
00:19:48,166 --> 00:19:52,125
Whatever I have to do, I'll get
those two to the Witch of Taboos.

381
00:19:52,166 --> 00:19:54,208
You truly are kind.

382
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,083
You think too much of me.

383
00:19:56,125 --> 00:20:00,041
I have a much more pragmatic reason
for adding them to our party as well.

384
00:20:00,041 --> 00:20:01,125
Which would be?

385
00:20:01,125 --> 00:20:03,166
Eve has been to the Land of Monsters before,

386
00:20:03,166 --> 00:20:05,166
and she has some connection to the witch.

387
00:20:06,041 --> 00:20:08,041
She'll make it easier to approach the witch.

388
00:20:08,041 --> 00:20:09,125
As for Lis...

389
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:13,083
They say the Witch of Taboos
is a dark elf, right?

390
00:20:13,083 --> 00:20:14,125
Oh, and so is Lis.

391
00:20:14,125 --> 00:20:18,208
Right. We'll be visitors who've
saved a young girl of her species.

392
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Play our cards right and we have
ourselves a favorable introduction.

393
00:20:22,041 --> 00:20:23,208
You've thought that far ahead...

394
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,125
Impressive, Sir Tooka.

395
00:20:25,166 --> 00:20:28,000
All primarily out
of self-interest, of course...

396
00:20:28,041 --> 00:20:31,125
But letting a girl like that
enjoy life with a smile

397
00:20:31,166 --> 00:20:34,208
is far better than
her quivering and crying.

398
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,041
Yes, I agree with that.

399
00:20:46,041 --> 00:20:48,041
Our pursuers are responding too quickly.

400
00:20:48,083 --> 00:20:49,166
How did they find out?

401
00:20:50,208 --> 00:20:54,083
I passed a man right before
leaving the bloodsport colosseum.

402
00:20:54,083 --> 00:20:55,083
Who?

403
00:20:55,166 --> 00:20:57,125
He called himself Muaji.

404
00:20:58,208 --> 00:21:01,000
I see. That group's boss, huh?

405
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,000
I'm sorry.

406
00:21:04,041 --> 00:21:07,166
I'm the reason you're all at risk
of such grave danger.

407
00:21:07,166 --> 00:21:08,166
Big Sis?

408
00:21:09,041 --> 00:21:10,125
Tooka, take Lis.

409
00:21:12,166 --> 00:21:14,125
You might be a bloodsport champion,

410
00:21:14,125 --> 00:21:16,166
but you have no chance
against those numbers solo.

411
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:17,166
Even so...

412
00:21:17,166 --> 00:21:22,041
Besides, what good would it do us to lose
our guide to the Witch of Taboos here?

413
00:21:22,208 --> 00:21:24,041
Then what do we do?

414
00:21:24,041 --> 00:21:25,041
We defeat them.

415
00:21:25,166 --> 00:21:27,125
I'll set a trap in advance.

416
00:21:37,125 --> 00:21:41,166
Just as you predicted,
the first wave is chasing after the horses.

417
00:21:41,166 --> 00:21:43,041
Were there any Ashint among them?

418
00:21:43,083 --> 00:21:45,083
No, I couldn't see any.

419
00:21:45,166 --> 00:21:48,125
The first wave was most likely
the duke's personal army.

420
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,041
Which means...

421
00:21:50,041 --> 00:21:52,208
that second wave might be Ashint.

422
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,000
We've succeeded in dividing them for now.

423
00:21:55,041 --> 00:21:59,125
Eve, you take Lis and hide
in the forest a little ways up ahead.

424
00:21:59,125 --> 00:22:01,083
I'll stand and fight with you.

425
00:22:01,083 --> 00:22:04,166
I need Seras for what I'm about to try next.

426
00:22:04,208 --> 00:22:06,125
So who will protect Lis?

427
00:22:07,208 --> 00:22:10,083
All right. I'll follow your lead.

428
00:22:10,125 --> 00:22:14,166
He was sharp enough to surmise his
enemy's plan from scant information.

429
00:22:14,208 --> 00:22:17,083
This Muaji guy is a smart one.

430
00:22:18,041 --> 00:22:19,000
Seras.

431
00:22:19,041 --> 00:22:20,000
Yes?

432
00:22:21,041 --> 00:22:23,041
I understand. I'll try it.

433
00:22:23,083 --> 00:22:25,166
Do you have a plan for beating so many foes?

434
00:22:26,041 --> 00:22:28,208
If you can't beat a foe head-on,

435
00:22:28,208 --> 00:22:31,208
drag them somewhere you can win.

436
00:22:36,166 --> 00:22:39,083
Now, let's get started.

437
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
DARK PLOT ~MISSING~

